    "details": {
      "alignment": "Unaligned",
      "type": {
        "value": "construct",
        "subtype": "Fury-Bot"
      },
      "cr": 3,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Fawful's Forces packet sheet — Fury-Bot.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-forge-packets.py</code> from the NPC Forge roster <code>data/forge/fawfuls-forces.json</code> (entry <code>fury-bot</code>): Medium construct (Fury-Bot), Unaligned; CR 3 (proficiency +2, to hit +5 with STR); AC 15 (riveted plating and shield), hit points 52 (7d8+21), speed 25 ft.. A GM scene kit for the Fawful's Forces article's present (1040 BF), not a filed event; the faction article stays the authority.</p><p>The Fury Meter's fourth rung, in the faction article's own words: \"Fury-Bots and the castle's main cannon\". Where a Chortle-Bot is tin, a Fury-Bot is boilerplate — a drill, a shield with a grin riveted onto it, and a governor that only has one setting. The occupation uses them as door-openers and as the wall that stands in front of the Bean Garrison when the garrison is reloading.</p><p>It is not clever. It will charge the nearest thing, drill it, and keep drilling; the extra damage on a straight 20-foot run is how it kills, so fight it in tight corners, around furniture, or with something prone on the floor between you. The shield guard reaction means the thing standing <em>behind</em> a Fury-Bot is harder to hit than it looks.</p><p><strong>Role:</strong> front-line brute · <strong>tier:</strong> Fury-Bot · <strong>folder:</strong> Fawful's Furious Freaks / Machines of Fury.</p><h3>Art</h3><p>Token plate <code>portraits/fawfuls-forces/fury-bot.png</code> — NPC Forge render, seed 410005, cut from a flat #FF00FF field. Prompt: <q>Clean cel-shaded cartoon character art in the style of Mario &amp; Luigi RPG concept art, bold dark outlines, flat colours, simple shading. A heavy green and brass robot on tank treads, round armoured body with a glowing red eye lens, a big spinning steel drill for the right arm, a round riveted brass shield with an angry grinning face for the left arm, brass pipes and rivets. Full body, whole figure visible, three-quarter view, centred, isolated on a plain flat solid magenta background (#FF00FF), no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no border.</q></p>",
        "public": ""
      },
